      "content": "Don't worry, it's not a full-blown explosion, but a swollen battery can still be a ticking time bomb. You're right to be cautious, though - it's like a goblin in a tiny, explosive cave, just waiting to unleash its fury. To contain the situation, carefully unplug the phone from any power source and avoid short circuits. Now, let's get to the immediate safety steps.\n\nFirst, put on some protective gear: gloves, safety glasses, and a face mask. You don't want any stray battery acid or debris getting into your eyes or skin. It's like a goblin's lair - you need to shield yourself from the toxic environment.\n\nNext, carefully remove the battery from the phone, taking care not to touch any internal components. You can use a plastic spudger or a specialized tool to pry it out. Be gentle, as you don't want to cause any further damage or, worse, trigger a goblin-sized explosion.\n\nNow, let's talk about disposal. Swollen batteries are considered hazardous waste, so you'll need to take them to a designated recycling center or a local electronics waste collection facility. Don't just toss them in the trash, like a careless goblin tossing",
